# Sales System — Git ignore policy
# See docs/GITHUB_INITIALIZATION_REPORT.md for the publication decision record.

# ── SECURITY: historical artifacts containing the retired GAS bearer URL ──
# These files are kept LOCALLY as marked historical evidence and MUST NEVER
# be committed. A clone or fork would redistribute the retired credential.
# Their 4 sidecar markers are excluded alongside them (kept locally only).
dev.zip
dev_phase24_rc_closed_2026-08-18.zip
mshop-diag.html
mshop-regression-test.html
dev.zip.SECURITY-RETIRED-DO-NOT-DISTRIBUTE.txt
dev_phase24_rc_closed_2026-08-18.zip.SECURITY-RETIRED-DO-NOT-DISTRIBUTE.txt
mshop-diag.html.SECURITY-RETIRED-DO-NOT-DISTRIBUTE.txt
mshop-regression-test.html.SECURITY-RETIRED-DO-NOT-DISTRIBUTE.txt
# Backstop: no local single-file build (may embed endpoints) enters git.
mshop-*.html
*.mshop

# ── Dependencies (reinstall with `npm ci`; package-lock.json IS tracked) ──
node_modules/

# ── Secrets / environment ──
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ── OS / editor / caches ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Local-only AI/tooling state (machine-specific paths, regenerable) ──
.claude/
.freebuff/
# Superpowers execution workspace: ledger, task briefs, review packages.
# Scratch for one plan's run; git history is the durable record.
.superpowers/

# ── Rust / Tauri build output ──
#
# Without these, `git add -A` would try to commit roughly 8.3 GB of build
# artifacts. `src-tauri/target` is additionally a directory junction to
# E:\Rust\targets on this machine, so it must never be followed into the index.
target/
src-tauri/target/
# Generated Android Studio / Gradle project. Regenerated by `tauri android init`
# and by any `tauri android build`.
src-tauri/gen/

# ── Frontend build output ──
dist/

# ── Local run logs / device evidence (regenerable, machine-local; PA) ──
*.log
*-evidence.txt
*-evidence-summary.txt
build-evidence-summary.txt
diagnosis-*.txt
step-report-*.txt
run-logcat*.txt
login-evidence.txt
adb-status-evidence.txt

# NOTE: `src-tauri/icons/` and `src-tauri/app-icon/` are deliberately NOT ignored.
# They are build inputs, not artifacts, so a fresh clone builds identically.
# The current set is a neutral placeholder until final branding is decided.

# ── Browser demo build (npm run build:demo); never shipped ──
dist-demo/
releases/

